# Design System Rules
- Fonts: Inter (Body/Headers), JetBrains Mono (Data/Metrics/Code).
- Colors:
  - Background: bg-slate-950 (#0B0F14)
  - Surface: bg-slate-900/50
  - Accent: text-cyan-400
  - Muted: text-slate-400
- Components: Use 'lucide-react' for icons. Use 'framer-motion' for animations.
- Layouts: Bento Grids, Split Screens, Terminal overlays. NO standard single-column blogs.

# Coding Standards
- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router).
- Styling: Tailwind CSS.
- Language: TypeScript (Strict).
- Components: Shadcn/UI pattern (Radix primitives).
- Animation: Framer Motion. Keep animations smooth and "mechanical" (easings), not bouncy.

# Special Instructions
1. When summarizing Research (MUCEDS, GVMP, LOKI), prioritize "Architecture", "Trade-offs", and "Technical Decisions".
2. When creating the "Hero" section, avoid human photos. Use abstract node/network topologies.
3. The "About" section is called "About & Experience".
4. Always separate "Research" (Academic/Simulations) from "Engineering" (Product/Web).
